Availability for a range means every night in that range must have remaining inventory — one night fully booked fails the whole range:

```java
boolean checkAvailability(String roomTypeId, LocalDate checkIn, LocalDate checkOut) {
    for (LocalDate date = checkIn; date.isBefore(checkOut); date = date.plusDays(1)) {
        RoomInventory inv = inventoryRepo.get(roomTypeId, date);
        if (inv.getRemainingCount() <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

This reads one row per night rather than scanning every existing `Booking` and computing overlaps on the fly — the pre-aggregated `RoomInventory` table is what keeps this a handful of indexed reads instead of an O(bookings) scan.
